# Root manifest for the LWS 1.0 client rules (YAML-LD, format 0.10.0).
#
# Client rules judge the exchanges an LWS client sends to a client session
# (CLIENT-TESTING.md, definitions/OBSERVATION.md). The server root manifest does not include
# this one: the server engine never runs a client rule, and the client service never runs a
# server test.
"@context":
  - ../context.jsonld
  - ../touchstone.jsonld
id: "#manifest"
type: Manifest
label: LWS 1.0 client rules
comment: >-
  Rules an LWS client's own traffic must satisfy, judged by Touchstone's client service as the
  developer drives the client against a session. Each included manifest covers one area of a
  session; a developer may declare an area out of scope.
specification:
  - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261005/
  - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-authn-ssi-cid-20260921/
  - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-authn-openid-20260803/
  - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-notifications-webhook/
  - https://w3c.github.io/lws-protocol/lws10-index/
include:
  - core.yamlld
  - authentication.yamlld
  - notifications.yamlld
  - index.yamlld
entries: []
